stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Ready
  Ready --> Reserved: Reserve bounded file
  Reserved --> Uploading: Upload bytes
  Uploading --> Verified: Hash and MIME verified
  Uploading --> Reserved: Upload fails and transaction rolls back
  Reserved --> Abandoned: Discard unuploaded file
  Verified --> Abandoned: Discard verified file
  Reserved --> Expired: Reservation deadline passes
  Verified --> Expired: Reservation deadline passes
  Verified --> Verified: Finalize fails and transaction rolls back
  Verified --> Filed: Finalize attachment
  Filed --> Filed: Replay finalize or read receipt
  Reserved --> Reserved: Replay reserve after lost response
  Abandoned --> Abandoned: Replay discard
  Expired --> Expired: Refuse upload or finalize
  Filed --> Filed: Refuse discard
%% never Filed without verified bytes
%% never More than one attachment for a reservation
%% never Receipt or upload for a non-visible deal
%% never Finalize after abandon or expiry
%% never Document listed as a publishable deliverable

%% All five never rules are checked in DocumentIntake.cfg, with counterexample mutations in check_model.py.
%% Abandoned and Expired both persist as the terminal expired state; their causes differ.
